      "en": "The 1716 Kangxi Dictionary sorted about 47,035 characters under 214 radicals, placing each character first by a shared graphic component and then by residual stroke count — a scheme that had cut Xu Shen's 540 radicals to 214 and still orders dictionaries today.",
